*-------------------------------------------------------------- 108 rpoem_driver
A lustful twig can twiddle up the tenderness of a spoon
And can kill the motion of wisdom.
But the brain beside gay power heals the action of earth
While the tenderness of a spoon heals the lustful twig.

A happy muffin shall bask under earth of night
And can ensnare the pond up charity of earth.
But the activity of charity strengthens sorrowful faith
While earth of night beseechs the happy muffin.

A wonton gate may gurgle under the gate of the age of a star
And should worship a gay shovel.
But frail wisdom ensnares the endurance of night
While the gate of the age of a star pursues the wonton gate.

A moody cloud shall ponder over the motion of a shovel
And should beseech the goodness of beauty.
But war over nature worships a wonton goat
While the motion of a shovel strengthens the moody cloud.

A gay book doth dance beside the dish within a sorrowful dog
And doth provoke sorrowful war.
But a moody spark becalms a rake of evil
While the dish within a sorrowful dog arouses the gay book.

A moody wagon wheel can simmer on power beside love
And can beseech the whistle beside the tenderness of a dove.
But the raven within love within piety provokes rusty faith
While power beside love heals the moody wagon wheel.

A gay spoon doth wiggle of the cloud under evil's duration
And shall understand the pond of moody wisdom.
But moody night beseechs the spoon in the gate on pensive land
While the cloud under evil's duration becalms the gay spoon.

A sorrowful goat should simmer on a gentle tree
And shall become a timid gate.
But the goodness of peace kills the age of nature
While a gentle tree becalms the sorrowful goat.

A gay dish must think under wonton heart
And should ensnare a frail spark.
But a brain of charity becalms a frolicking petal
While wonton heart understands the gay dish.

A timorous flower shall whistle under the notion of a star
And may heal the feeling of a trap.
But timid time worships the motion of charity
While the notion of a star pursues the timorous flower.

A frail petal shall tumble beside nature's feeling
And should becalm power's feeling.
But the taste of a star arouses timorous war
While nature's feeling strengthens the frail petal.
